NAME
       sync - write data waiting in memory to the disks

SYNOPSIS
       sync [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
       Linux keeps recently written data in memory for a short time before it
       goes to disk, which makes writing fast. sync makes the kernel write all
       of it out now (or only the data of the files named). Use it before
       pulling out a USB disk or before forcing a machine off. A normal
       shutdown or umount does this by itself.

EXAMPLES
           cp /root/backup.tar /mnt/usb/ && sync

SEE ALSO
       umount(8), shutdown(8)
